A||||4||Fiero_24||I need info on tranny cooler/do they work?||||6||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||10-14-2001||04:21 PM||||I am interested in a tranny cooler for my 3 speed auto.  Has anyone tried these?  Do they help at all?  What kind should I use?<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||6
Z||000001||Bob||10-14-2001||04:56 PM||||I have one on my Grand Prix, it works well at keeping the tranny cooler than normal (heat kills autos). I got mine from <A HREF="http://www.grandprixstore.com." TARGET=_blank>www.grandprixstore.com.</A>  It wasnt that expensive, but it doesnt have a fan on it.<P>------------------<BR>1997 Pontiac Grand Prix GTP -lotsa mods, so little room...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||10-14-2001||05:49 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I am buying mine from <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  with a fan.  I planned on relocating the battery to the front and putting the cooler right under the vent where the battery is.  Of course I am adding more vents since the passenger side one will be blocked by a tranny cooler.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-14-2001||06:57 PM||||You can use a heater core from a wrecking yard for next to nothing. I have one for my oil cooler behind the scoop on the right side of my car.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SKIDMARK||10-14-2001||07:20 PM||||A tranny cooler is a good idea. Adds some life to the trans, especially in a hot climate. I've seen kits in parts stores for about $60 that should work with minor mods. The problem is finding a good place to mount it. Mounting it on the front of the radiator kind of defeats the purpose of trying to make things run cooler. If you have functional scoops on the panels behind the doors, that would be a good place. <BR> <P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
